# PacketYeeter Analyzer Configuration
# Copy to /etc/default/packetyeeter-analyzer

# gRPC listen address for collectors
LISTEN_ADDR=0.0.0.0:9090

# Prometheus metrics HTTP listen address. Bind to loopback or a trusted
# management network unless Prometheus reaches this host over protected links.
METRICS_ADDR=:9091

# GeoIP ASN database path
GEOIP_ASN_PATH=/var/lib/GeoIP/GeoLite2-ASN.mmdb

# Optional: GeoLite2-Country.mmdb or GeoLite2-City.mmdb for country-level
# enrichment (powers the Inspector's "Threats by Country" panel). Not set by
# default since it requires a separate MaxMind download; add it via
# EXTRA_ARGS below if you have one, e.g.:
#   EXTRA_ARGS=-geoip-country /var/lib/GeoIP/GeoLite2-Country.mmdb

# Threat intelligence uses the free, keyless Shodan InternetDB API (no API key required)

# All optional/conditional analyzer flags go through EXTRA_ARGS. The unit
# file's ExecStart uses plain systemd variable substitution only (no bash
# ${VAR:+...} conditionals - systemd does not run ExecStart through a shell
# and does not support that syntax), so combine every optional flag you want
# into a single EXTRA_ARGS line, e.g.:
#   EXTRA_ARGS=-dry-run -reputation-threshold 75 -v
#
# Operational safety: start new deployments with -dry-run, keep the inspector
# on loopback or behind trusted access controls, and enable pprof only briefly.
# EXTRA_ARGS=-dry-run -inspect-addr 127.0.0.1:9092

# Reputation thresholds and score caps (0 = uncapped). Defaults leave headroom
# above -reputation-threshold while bounding runaway penalty accumulation.
# EXTRA_ARGS=-reputation-threshold 75 -reputation-ip-score-cap 200 -reputation-ja4-score-cap 200 -reputation-asn-score-cap 500

# TLS / mTLS on the gRPC listener (off by default = plaintext). -tls-client-ca
# requires client certificates; -control-client-names limits PushRules and
# WatchDecisions to those certificate names. Files are re-read when they change.
# See docs/operations.md#tls-and-mtls.
# EXTRA_ARGS=-tls-cert /etc/packetyeeter/tls/analyzer.crt -tls-key /etc/packetyeeter/tls/analyzer.key -tls-client-ca /etc/packetyeeter/tls/ca.crt -control-client-names controller.example.net
#
# gRPC connections are closed after -grpc-max-connection-age (default 1h; 0 =
# never) plus -grpc-max-connection-age-grace for open streams, so clients
# re-handshake against rotated certificates and CA bundles.
# EXTRA_ARGS=-grpc-max-connection-age 1h -grpc-max-connection-age-grace 30s

# Enable verbose logging
# EXTRA_ARGS=-v
#
# Runtime rules for scrub collectors (PushRules). Off by default: the gRPC
# listener is unauthenticated unless mTLS (-tls-client-ca) is configured, so
# restrict PushRules with -control-client-names (see above) or firewall
# -listen-addr to trusted controllers and collectors before enabling it.
# EXTRA_ARGS=-enable-rule-api
#
# Keep pushed rules across analyzer restarts (otherwise a restart clears the
# scrub collectors' rules until the controller pushes again). The unit can
# write /var/lib/packetyeeter.
# EXTRA_ARGS=-enable-rule-api -rule-state-dir /var/lib/packetyeeter

# Runtime enforcement kill switch: POST /api/enforcement/stop on the inspector
# suppresses every enforcing command from every detector, immediately, without a
# restart, while leaving detection and reporting running. Unblock/allowlist
# commands keep flowing. It is one-way - resuming requires a config change and a
# restart. This is why -inspect-addr should stay reachable to operators but not
# to the internet.

# Sustained-download detection: catches clients that pull an unusual amount of
# data, or walk an unusual breadth of resources, over a sliding window. Rate
# limits cannot see this - a scraper under every per-second limit that sustains
# it for an hour is invisible to them and obvious over five minutes.
#
# Off by default, and enabling detection does not enable blocking. Run it with
# -sustained-enabled alone first and tune the thresholds against
# /api/sustained in the inspector, which reports for each client which
# thresholds it is under and how close it is to them. Add -sustained-enforce
# only once the would-block set looks right.
#
# The volume path additionally needs -egress-accounting on the collectors.
# EXTRA_ARGS=-sustained-enabled
# EXTRA_ARGS=-sustained-enabled -sustained-enforce -sustained-min-bytes 5368709120

# Decision stream for a controller (scrub mode): WatchDecisions streams every
# command sent to collectors, campaign observations and scrub fingerprints.
# Off by default. The gRPC listener is unauthenticated unless mTLS
# (-tls-client-ca) is configured, so restrict WatchDecisions with
# -control-client-names (see TLS above) or enable it only when LISTEN_ADDR is
# reachable from trusted networks alone.
# EXTRA_ARGS=-enable-watch-api -watch-max-subscribers 16 -watch-buffer-size 10000
